    "note": "Points carry R+T+A = 1 to within 2e-16. Most come from the run made after the percent, circular-atom and cross-polarization fixes; the exceptions are listed under 'older_points'.",
    "older_points": "1D m=1000 and the 2D points above (10,10) predate the last run, whose per-solve budget cut the sweep short. The 1D ones and C1's (15,15) / (20,20) come from the earlier percent-era run, rescaled -- valid, because those cases were never touched by the circular-atom or cross-polarization bugs. C1b (15,15)/(20,20) and C2 (15,15)/(20,20)/(30,30) are the original manual Moose entries.",
    "validation": "1D (groups A, B, D1) reproduces the original manual Moose entries to all six recorded digits. 2D lands nearest the well-factorized references of benchmark/night_run_2: C1 0.39871 vs Pol 0.38896 / Li 0.38996 / NV 0.39065; C2 0.67136 vs Li 0.67233; D2 0.90485 vs Li 0.91802. C1b and D2 are still rising at (10,10) (nG=441) and are not converged there.",
    "manual_baseline_superseded": "C1b_Si_pillars_diffract held the manual entries up to (10,10) while the script's first run was rejected for lost cross-polarized flux. The fixed run agrees with those manual values to under 2% from (4,4) up and replaces them."
